{
  "name": "gonzalez_as4_8552_cai",
  "kind": "measured",
  "reference": "E.V. Gonzalez Juan, 'Simulation of interlaminar and intralaminar damage in polymer-based composites for aeronautical applications under impact loading', PhD thesis, Universitat de Girona, 2010 (deposited 2011), http://hdl.handle.net/10803/22834 (TDX, open access), Chapters 3-4: Table 3.12 (laminates, cured ply and plate thickness), Tables 3.4, 3.7, 3.8 (impact energy, impactor mass), Table 4.3 (C-scan projected delamination areas), Tables 4.4 and 4.8 (CAI failure loads), Tables 4.9 and 4.13 (CAI strengths), Figs. 4.17 and 4.32 (maximum indentation printed over each contour plot). The L02-L04 tests are also reported in Gonzalez, Maimi, Camanho, Lopes & Blanco, 'Effects of ply clustering in laminated composite plates under low-velocity impact loading', Compos Sci Technol 71 (2011) 805-817, doi:10.1016/j.compscitech.2010.12.018, and simulated in Gonzalez, Maimi, Camanho, Turon & Mayugo, 'Simulation of drop-weight impact and compression after impact tests on composite laminates', Compos Struct 94 (2012) 3364-3378, doi:10.1016/j.compstruct.2012.05.015; only the thesis was read in full. Hexply AS4/8552 tape; 150 x 100 mm coupons impacted in a CEAST Fractovis drop tower on the ASTM D7136 125 x 75 mm window (four rubber-tipped clamps) with a 16 mm (R = 8 mm) hemispherical steel impactor; CAI in an ASTM D7137 fixture. Four laminates of 32-36 plies: quasi-isotropic L02 [(45/0/-45/90)4]s, ply-clustered L03 [(45_2/0_2/-45_2/90_2)2]s and L04 [45_4/0_4/-45_4/90_4]s (the same in-plane layup), cross-ply L06 [(0/90)9]s, each at 38.6, 28.6 and 19.3 J (5 kg); plus the 48-ply quasi-isotropic L05 at 38.6 J (5 kg) and 58 J (6 and 15 kg). Every value is transcribed from a table or the text; none is digitized from a plot. Strength = F_fc / (b h) with the nominal width b = 100 mm and the cured plate thickness h of Table 3.12, as the thesis does (its Tables 4.9 and 4.13 print the result a factor 10 low, e.g. 16.6 for 96 kN / (100 x 5.8 mm) = 165.5 MPa). Per-specimen thickness and width are not reported. C-scan areas are tabulated for L02-L04 only; the L06 and L05 C-scans are images without a scale and are not digitized. Dents are the maximum indentation printed over each contour plot (3D coordinate measuring machine), carried only where the plotted specimen is the CAI specimen. No undamaged (pristine) compression strength is reported. The 16-ply L01 (3.0 mm) is left out: the thesis reports global buckling in the CAI fixture, its 197 MPa (Table 4.13) is near the plate's buckling stress, and its specimen is not named.",
